WEBVTT

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.030
Come on.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:47.870
- This is Texas, isn't it, stranger? - Has been for some time.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:51.800
I must be getting closer to Border City then.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:55.840
You go on down the road till you come to Big Sycamore Tree down there, then you turn left.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:00.000
- Uh-huh. How far is it? - Oh, no more direction.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Oh, thanks very, very much.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:11.240
Thank you.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:04.840
Punch it!

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:32.790
I know.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.550
In case he's badly wounded, perhaps we should leave him on the next branch.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.540
It's all right, I...

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:56.310
Joe, I don't think this is a safe place to keep your money.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.830
Hey Ranger, howdy Slim.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:18.390
Ranger, uh, are you the sheriff or something like that?

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.390
Something like that.

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:21.340
Well, uh, sir, I have a complaint to make.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.340
Complaint?

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:26.340
Yes, sir, last night in this town there were a lot of men shooting guns and they put and wrecked my wagon and I almost got shot.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.490
Where?

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:28.490
Where? All over, that's where.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.000
Broke your butt?

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:33.030
That's too bad. Go get yourself some water, Sonny.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:41.420
My partner broke my wagon and...

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:46.640
Hey, that's a pretty good trick.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:49.470
I'd like to buy a horse like that and trade in this outfit of mine.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.490
No, Sonny's not for sale. You better see Boots Crawley.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:53.380
Boots Crawley? Who's he?

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.380
He runs a livery stable down the street.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:56.230
Oh, good.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:57.230
But you won't find him there.

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:59.240
During business hours, he's generally in the saloon.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.230
- Hi, Joe. - Hello, Hank.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:10.910
- They're waiting for you inside. - Yeah, who's they?

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:14.280
- Captain of the Mexican council. - Sort of figured.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:20.630
Oh, this is the fifth time he's crossed over the border in the last five months.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:23.780
He brings a big gang of men, hits one of these small towns...

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.850
back over the border before half the town can get his pants on.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:30.000
Nelson's the twelfth man he's killed. About time somebody did something.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:31.780
- Hi. - Don't look at me.

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:34.120
- Howdy, Senor Muñoz. - Senor Warder.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:37.660
The Mexican government has sent troops twice

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:40.000
against El Tigre and his bandits.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.610
They just fade away into the mountains.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.250
Since then, we've sent three of the best men

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:47.570
in the Mexican Secret Service.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:48.980
They disappear.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:53.300
Finally, we sent Colonel Sanchez, the chief of the Bureau.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.000
You hear that, Joe? You'd have help.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.630
What happened to Colonel Sanchez?

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:00.000
He hasn't been heard from.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:06.380
- You plan to send Senor Warder in alone? - I'm planning to visit my sister in St. Louis.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:10.080
Oh, now, now. Joe Warder's my best and most experienced ranger.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:13.920
If you fix up the government technicalities, he'll get L.T. Gray.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.420
Joe don't know the meaning of fear.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.880
That's a lot of bull, Captain.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:20.000
I'm not something big out of one of Beatle's nickel and dime novels.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.000
- You come here. - Where?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:28.130
Those are the San Clementes, 50 miles from here to the foothills.

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.000
Another 10 miles from here to the foothills.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.500
- Ten miles into the heart of the mountains

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:32.620
is the village of San Clemente.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:33.460
- Yeah.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:36.080
- Full of the toughest thugs and riffraff from both countries.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:36.920
- I know.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:37.760
- I know.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:39.750
I've been there, and they know me.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.230
- Well, Joey, you'd have one advantage.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:42.270
- What do you want me to do?

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:43.810
- Pick up the tiger in my saddlebag

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:45.270
and ride him gently back here?

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.650
If I'd be so full of holes, you could take his picture through me.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.210
- No, just get yourself back here alive.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:52.390
The rewards don't say nothing about him being alive,

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.310
and they're good in both countries.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:58.360
- The advantage the captain spoke of was this.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.000
We have learned till Tigris held

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:07.040
comes into the town only for raids but he has a trusted lieutenant an American

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:12.590
Señor Omor. Oh I see Omor. Well that's nice that's a great help you want the

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:18.520
lieutenant too? No I... My idea is that any countryman of yours who will sell

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:26.540
himself to El Tigre might sell El Tigre to his countrymen. Am I under orders? Oh no

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.730
Joe no I can't order you out of the country you'd have to volunteer.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.620
- Well, I couldn't volunteer, not right now.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:34.230
- Why not?

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:41.370
- Thirsty, got to get me a drink.

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.050
- Where'd you get that hat, fella?

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:50.730
- What'd you do, son, walk?

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:55.430
- Looks like I could walk a lot better.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.460
- What ranch are you from, Doc?

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.840
- Hey, some dude, eh?

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:00.000
- Hey, did any of you come here?

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:04.030
You fellas see that Boots what's-his-name sell me that horse and tell me he was broken in?

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.030
Broken what?

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:06.840
Broken in and gentle.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:08.840
He took my money and my board buck.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:09.840
Took his board buck, huh?

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:10.840
Look, you're all witnesses.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.840
I'm going inside and bring him out here and make him eat his words.

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:14.720
Stand back. I'll be out in a second.

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:29.350
I wish to goodness you wouldn't bother me, son, when I'm drinking.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:32.820
Stop your dukes.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:34.860
Come on, I'm ready.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:35.860
Just a minute, son.

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:38.120
I'm glad you stopped me, Sheriff.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.120
You boys are disturbing the peace.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:40.120
I ain't.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:41.120
He's sold me a wild horse.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.120
Nellie's a gentle horse, like a mother.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.120
A man should have some legal protection.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.120
Now, wait a minute.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:47.120
Maybe the horse needs some protection.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:51.380
I think Nellie's been broke to distrust a certain class of people.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.380
What do you mean?

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.400
Suppose you try to get on her from this side.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.960
From this side?

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.960
She won't buck me again, will she?

00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:00.000
No, you just put your trust in the law, son.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:03.530
Now, hold her. Don't let her buck me.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:08.500
Buck before.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.970
What do you know?

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:13.640
Come here, Sonny.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:14.680
Oh, now.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.910
You wouldn't like to trade horses, would you, Ranger?

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:18.910
No. Where I'm going, I'm liable to need, Sonny.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:20.800
Yeah. Well, I'll keep this one, then.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.840
Ah.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:25.550
You wait here, Sonny. I'll bring you a glass of beer.

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:27.040
Come on, folks.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.340
Crawley's by him.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:29.350
Huh?

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:42.480
I won't ride down to the river with you, Joe. I might attract attention.

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:48.010
Looks like we already attracted some.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:55.150
Yeah, not bad. Anything more I can do for you, Joe?

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:57.450
Other side of the border ain't much you can do, Captain.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:58.290
No.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.160
I'll see.

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:02.310
Keep it shiny, will you?

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:05.990
Bye, Joan. Don't say that, Captain.

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:02.120
This ain't him.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:03.880
How you know?

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:04.850
Too young.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:06.630
What do we do?

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:09.570
We don't want this fella.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:37.520
- What happened? - Some fellas jumped you.

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:40.470
- Fellas jumped me? What for? - Don't you know?

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:45.170
Look, mister, the only thing I know around here is that no matter what happens, I fall off a horse.

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:50.100
Oh, ow, ow. Why would they want to jump me?

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:53.130
Well, they probably got you mixed up with somebody else.

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:56.500
Yeah, well, thanks anyway, mister.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:14:00.000
- How come you were following me? - Believe it or not, I was trying to find out which...

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.010
Which way you headed?

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:04.000
A place called San Clemente.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:06.160
Ever heard of it?

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:08.560
Yeah, I've heard of it.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:11.000
Maybe I'll ride along with you for a piece.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.000
Sure wouldn't take you out of your way any?

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:15.610
Not much.

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:19.590
You seem to have a habit of getting mixed up with fellas who are bigger than you are.

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:21.450
Fellas, not only fellas, but girls too.

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:23.450
- Girls? - Sure. I get all the big ones.

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:27.590
There was a girl called Mary Martha McGuire.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:28.040
She...

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.910
- See what I mean? - Come here, Sonny!

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:40.660
And then there was Peg. I guess she loved me more, a lot more than all the rest of them.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:46.870
But was she jealous? Oh boy. All she had to do was see me looking at a picture of a girl in a magazine and wham!

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:50.740
And when she landed, Joe, there was 195 pounds behind it.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:54.640
Well, it's getting too hot to travel. Let's rest here a while.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:58.130
Then I'll set you on the trail. I'm going a different way. My business is private.

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:17.130
All right, sonny, go get yourself some water.

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:21.700
Okay, Nellie, get yourself some water.

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:24.230
No, not grass, water.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:42.560
You asleep?

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:48.140
I was just thinking if you should come into San Clemente while I'm there.

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.310
I'd like you to meet my brother.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:53.450
You got a brother in San Clemente?

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:53.850
Mm-hmm.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:55.260
His name is Patrick.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.540
I haven't seen him for eight years.

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:57.640
Runs a silver mine.

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:00.000
Did your brother send for you?

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:02.030
Not exactly.

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:03.840
In fact, he told me not to come at all.

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:06.190
I thought I'd go out and surprise him.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:09.900
He's been running the mine for eight years, huh?

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:12.650
Ever since his second year, he's been sending money home every month.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:15.010
Wonderful presents to Mom, my sister.

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:18.880
Well, I haven't been doing anything in New York, so I thought I'd go out and help him with the mine.

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:20.520
He must be doing pretty well.

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:22.000
Pretty well?

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:25.860
Patrick, he's the kind of a guy that always did everything better than anybody else.

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:29.320
He's always the biggest, strongest, handsomest.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.960
The pride at 10th Avenue.

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:36.090
There's only one to a family like him.

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:38.070
I guess Patrick was it for the O'Moors.

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:39.940
O'Moors?

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:43.780
We've been riding along together and didn't even know each other's last name.

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:45.780
My name is J. Dennis O'Moors.

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:46.610
Joe Warder.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:47.610
Glad to know you, Joe.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:51.520
You know, I may go along to San Clemente with you after all.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:52.510
Good, good.

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:59.700
There she is, Denny.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:04.180
- This is where we send all his mail to.

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:08.770
- Oh, that's on the other side of town to the west.

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:11.870
We'll ride around and wait till after dark to go in.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:14.000
This is kind of a tough town, Denny.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:17.020
- Wait till you see the expression

00:17:17.020 --> 00:17:20.320
on Patrick O'Moore's face when he sees us.

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:34.200
- Senor? - Yes.

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:41.360
- Muchachos? - Gracias, senor.

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:52.640
- You get him? - No, senor.

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:53.460
No.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:55.920
But the wait was there were two of them, two of them.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:59.730
- Another ranger? - No, senor.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.000
You see, senor?

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.080
When will he be here?

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:03.080
Tonight he should be.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:03.970
But wait, what?

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:04.950
I'm not interested.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:05.950
Report to El Tigre.

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:07.450
But I'd like it to explain, senor.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:08.450
Senor Amor said move on.

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:10.300
Do you wish to discuss the matter?

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:11.300
No, senor.

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:12.120
Then move on.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:14.120
I suggest you let Berger go after water.

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:15.120
He ought to be able to handle him.

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:16.120
Yes, I can get there, all right?

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:19.360
I'll give you your instructions later.

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:20.360
Yes, sir.

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:23.210
This may become a matter for El Tigre himself.

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:25.100
This may become a matter for El Tigre himself.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:28.550
Yes, sir.

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:30.000
This may become a matter for El Tigre himself.

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:34.450
- So, how many men are you here? - Ten, or twelve.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:38.450
The next hour or so will be at the Casa Alvarado.

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:41.620
Meanwhile, keep your eyes open for Senor Ward and his friend.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:45.520
I assume you will not wish to be disturbed at the home of the beautiful Senorita.

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:47.480
You assume wrong.

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:51.640
Let me know the minute Warder arrives.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:53.650
Yes, Senor.

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:10.240
That will be all. Thank you. There he is now.

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:13.940
Please be careful, Carmelita. Remember, we're in trouble.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:17.130
I am in trouble. He does not want you, Mama.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:21.000
Senor Patrick O'Moore.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:24.360
Senor. Senora. Senorita.

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:27.150
You will excuse me. I will not excuse you.

00:19:27.150 --> 00:19:28.070
Carmelita.

00:19:32.490 --> 00:19:37.850
- Please be seated, sir. - Thank you.

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:40.590
- Would the senor like some chocolates? - No, thank you.

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:50.800
Beware at me.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:54.630
Perhaps Senor O'Mur does not know that in our country this is rude.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.780
Oh, yes, I know. But your daughter was rude to me.

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:02.660
- Why are you so crazy about me, Carmelita?

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:06.070
- I don't know, but I adore you.

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:10.500
You have such a beautiful red nose, Carmelita.

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.230
- Drinking isn't one of my vices, Carmel.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:15.560
Maybe you are.

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:16.900
Maybe there is something vicious

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.740
about the way I like to stare at you.

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:21.000
Maybe if your mother weren't here,

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:22.640
I'd tell you what an unholy desire

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:24.840
I had to lock that small body of yours in--

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:26.180
- Senor.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:28.240
- In holy matrimony.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.920
In fact, I've been talking to the Padre.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.940
I'm sure he did not give you absolution.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:35.960
It is not wine I see on your nose, senor amor.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.530
It is blood.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:40.450
You talk too much, Carmelita.

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:41.450
I won't like that in a wife.

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:44.370
Your father and his interests got along all right with me till the day he died.

00:20:44.370 --> 00:20:47.120
My father died of acute indigestion.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:50.140
His heart could not digest you and El Tigre.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:51.580
Some people would say...

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:54.580
Some people would say his daughter and I could go a long way in this part of Mexico.

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:55.600
And we will.

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:59.440
I don't ask for things, Carmel.

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:05.280
- Not even from their people? - We have his blessing.

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:09.480
Then why do you ask to marry me? Why don't you take me?

00:21:09.480 --> 00:21:14.090
Like a bag of silver. Like a girl from the market.

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:16.960
Maybe I will.

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:31.990
Uh, Kenny.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:30.000
Is this number seven, Buena Vista?

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:37.120
- Patrick O'MoR. - Patrick O'MoR.

00:22:37.200 --> 00:22:43.970
- This is number seven, isn't it? - Not here. Nobody knows him.

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:49.630
Not here? I've been writing to him here for years.

00:22:49.710 --> 00:22:54.210
- Go away. - Go away? Joe, did you hear what this guy says?

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:56.750
- He wants me to go away. - I said you go away.

00:22:56.830 --> 00:23:00.000
- You pull a shiv on me and I'll break your... - Danny, don't...

00:23:00.030 --> 00:23:06.420
Well Joe, I've come 3,000 miles to see my brother, I'm not going to be stopped the last ten feet.

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:10.140
How I know you are his brother.

00:23:10.140 --> 00:23:11.270
Oh.

00:23:11.270 --> 00:23:14.010
How would I know this address?

00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:15.930
How would I know where to send his mail?

00:23:15.930 --> 00:23:16.880
Who...

00:23:16.880 --> 00:23:17.830
Who'd have...

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:20.770
Who'd have showed me this place?

00:23:20.770 --> 00:23:24.380
Hello.

00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:27.290
Hello.

00:23:27.290 --> 00:23:28.270
Well, you see Joe?

00:23:28.270 --> 00:23:30.000
A hundred and ninety-five pounds if she's...

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.550
You go to Casa Contreras on the other side of town.

00:23:33.650 --> 00:23:34.570
Why do you talk?

00:23:34.670 --> 00:23:36.070
He's cute.

00:23:36.170 --> 00:23:38.350
Casa Contreras, huh?

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:39.320
Muchas gracias.

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:42.100
Look, if you'd have told us that in the first place,

00:23:42.200 --> 00:23:43.500
you'd have saved an awful lot of time.

00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:45.500
Gracias, amigo, senorita.

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:49.580
Come on, Denny.

00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:54.800
Brother of yours seems to be right well known around here.

00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:57.270
When he hears about this caretaker, he'll fix him.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.000
- Here's the place. - Well, this does anything?

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:35.950
How about it, Joe? You want to come in for a minute and meet him?

00:24:35.950 --> 00:24:36.950
You don't have to stay long.

00:24:36.950 --> 00:24:39.870
No, not tonight, son. I'll drop by in the morning, maybe.

00:24:39.870 --> 00:24:40.690
You go on in.

00:24:40.690 --> 00:24:42.950
I'll see you later, cowboy.

00:24:42.950 --> 00:24:46.500
Uh, I'm looking for a Mr. Patrick O'Moore.

00:24:46.500 --> 00:24:47.490
Does he live here?

00:24:47.490 --> 00:24:50.080
Hey, well, don't close the door on me.

00:24:50.080 --> 00:24:53.460
Well, that's better.

00:25:05.280 --> 00:25:06.720
- Howdy. - Hi.

00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:09.460
- Will you get some more, senor? - Will I?

00:25:09.460 --> 00:25:10.920
- Yeah. - Just watch me.

00:25:10.920 --> 00:25:14.420
Ah, how's that, huh?

00:25:14.420 --> 00:25:15.450
Not bad, huh?

00:25:15.450 --> 00:25:18.400
The second time in my life I've ever got off a horse and I've been fucked off.

00:25:18.400 --> 00:25:19.480
A minute to go at it.

00:25:19.480 --> 00:25:21.960
- Right over! - No!

00:25:21.960 --> 00:25:29.730
Easy with him.

00:25:30.280 --> 00:25:35.320
Don't hurt him.

00:26:36.490 --> 00:26:37.080
It's up.

00:27:27.420 --> 00:27:30.000
But no, by this time, that Senor Amor is not interested

00:27:34.700 --> 00:27:37.400
Sometimes I wonder what makes you men so stupid.

00:27:37.400 --> 00:27:40.700
Capitan, the little man said he was his brother.

00:27:40.700 --> 00:27:42.060
How am I going to know?

00:27:42.060 --> 00:27:43.460
No matter who the man said he was,

00:27:43.460 --> 00:27:47.490
you had no right to give this address.

00:27:47.490 --> 00:27:48.410
What's wrong?

00:27:48.410 --> 00:27:49.750
I come quick.

00:27:49.750 --> 00:27:50.600
I tell you.

00:27:50.600 --> 00:27:51.530
You'll catch him.

00:27:51.530 --> 00:27:52.560
What else do you want?

00:27:52.560 --> 00:27:54.230
The man that was with him.

00:27:54.230 --> 00:27:57.320
The man that was with him was obviously Warder, the ranger.

00:27:57.320 --> 00:28:00.000
And that's the matter that calls for an explanation.

00:28:00.760 --> 00:28:01.930
- There's the senor.

00:28:01.930 --> 00:28:04.390
Now you'll catch it.

00:28:04.390 --> 00:28:10.760
Are you told to keep your mouth shut or not?

00:28:10.760 --> 00:28:12.050
- Si, senor.

00:28:12.050 --> 00:28:13.760
I always keep my mouth shut.

00:28:13.760 --> 00:28:16.540
It was my sister, the fat one.

00:28:16.540 --> 00:28:17.600
What can I do?

00:28:17.600 --> 00:28:19.410
He says he's your brother.

00:28:19.410 --> 00:28:21.530
- Says he's my brother?

00:28:21.530 --> 00:28:22.900
- Si, senor.

00:28:22.900 --> 00:28:24.530
I don't say anything otherwise.

00:28:24.530 --> 00:28:27.590
If he says he's your brother, what can I do?

00:28:27.590 --> 00:28:28.710
- What'd he look like?

00:28:28.710 --> 00:28:30.000
- Well, he's your brother.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:33.590
- He's young, he's short, but very tough, senor.

00:28:33.590 --> 00:28:34.980
Right away, he wants to fight.

00:28:34.980 --> 00:28:37.110
- Why'd he come to you?

00:28:37.110 --> 00:28:40.820
- Not to me, senor, to the house, where the letters come.

00:28:40.820 --> 00:28:42.530
- Yeah.

00:28:42.530 --> 00:28:43.530
- Wait a minute, lay off me!

00:28:43.530 --> 00:28:44.510
- Where is he now?

00:28:44.510 --> 00:28:46.190
- Patrick, it's me, Danny!

00:28:46.190 --> 00:28:49.830
Patrick, it's me, Danny, look!

00:28:49.830 --> 00:28:51.910
Look what they've done to me, they put handcuffs on me!

00:28:51.910 --> 00:28:53.620
Tell these guys to get them off!

00:28:53.620 --> 00:28:57.550
Patrick, Patrick!

00:28:57.550 --> 00:29:00.000
- You seem to have mentioned

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.780
- You've made a mistake, mister.

00:29:01.780 --> 00:29:03.420
- I haven't made any mistake.

00:29:03.420 --> 00:29:05.700
I know that boy's any place.

00:29:05.700 --> 00:29:07.630
Patrick, I know you're here.

00:29:07.630 --> 00:29:08.470
What have they done to you?

00:29:08.470 --> 00:29:10.770
They do the same thing to you that they did to me?

00:29:10.770 --> 00:29:12.130
Wait a minute, lay off me!

00:29:12.130 --> 00:29:13.310
Will you please?

00:29:13.310 --> 00:29:20.660
Look, you hurt my brother and I'll kick your brains out!

00:29:20.660 --> 00:29:22.830
- Send him away back to the border.

00:29:22.830 --> 00:29:23.990
Send a couple of men with him.

00:29:23.990 --> 00:29:24.830
- Si, senor.

00:29:24.830 --> 00:29:26.510
- Tell him not to hurt him.

00:29:26.510 --> 00:29:27.790
And warn him he's not to try to come back

00:29:27.790 --> 00:29:30.000
unless he wants to get into serious trouble.

00:29:30.540 --> 00:29:32.900
- Now, right away. - Si, senor.

00:29:33.510 --> 00:29:37.170
To satisfy your curiosity, I have no brother.

00:29:37.320 --> 00:29:39.150
Si, senor.

00:29:40.100 --> 00:29:42.950
Sit down.

00:29:44.480 --> 00:29:47.380
- Please, senor! Please! - You are told not to talk to anybody!

00:29:47.480 --> 00:29:49.110
Don't forget it again!

00:29:50.150 --> 00:29:51.670
Now, get out!

00:29:54.220 --> 00:29:57.840
So, you are going to take care of Senor Water.

00:29:58.900 --> 00:30:00.000
- Where is he now? - Definitely.

00:30:00.030 --> 00:30:03.370
Believe me, senor. I've got twenty men covering the town this town.

00:30:03.370 --> 00:30:04.960
All right, you fathead. Listen again.

00:30:04.960 --> 00:30:07.310
This is a dangerous man we're after.

00:30:07.310 --> 00:30:09.830
If you let him get within five hundred yards of El Tigre,

00:30:09.830 --> 00:30:12.500
don't bother to come back later with any excuses.

00:30:12.500 --> 00:30:13.990
I'll get him, senor.

00:30:13.990 --> 00:30:15.840
Shut that door and wait below.

00:30:15.840 --> 00:30:17.090
Si, senor.

00:30:17.090 --> 00:30:19.800
If he's not back by ten o'clock, call me.

00:30:40.650 --> 00:30:45.020
Grab it, cowboy. Hands flat on the table and don't move them.

00:30:45.020 --> 00:30:52.120
And don't holler. I'm a very nervous man. I can't stand the noises.

00:30:52.120 --> 00:30:53.120
Where's your Texas badge?

00:30:53.120 --> 00:30:56.270
I left it down the drugstore.

00:30:56.270 --> 00:30:59.960
It won't do you any good here anyway. Can I arrest somebody?

00:31:00.860 --> 00:31:07.040
shoot somebody how do you think you'd ever get out of here i was thinking you'd take me out talk

00:31:07.040 --> 00:31:13.660
nicely to them fellas tell them we're going to go see el tigre 20 men around this house they work

00:31:13.660 --> 00:31:18.630
for el tigre not for me they've got a certain respect for you mister and so have i i'm not

00:31:18.630 --> 00:31:22.440
going out of here with a bag over my head like your little brother listen water you're a man

00:31:22.440 --> 00:31:30.000
he's a kid i sent him back where he's safe from you from me i'm a businessman i came down

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:31.490
I need to run a silver mine.

00:31:31.490 --> 00:31:34.770
Like everybody else, I was robbed blind by every little bandit in these mountains.

00:31:34.770 --> 00:31:41.270
Then I found El Tigre, a tiger.

00:31:41.270 --> 00:31:44.110
There are no more little bandits now.

00:31:44.110 --> 00:31:45.840
You found him and hooked up with him.

00:31:45.840 --> 00:31:46.850
Your head's in his mouth.

00:31:46.850 --> 00:31:48.630
I make certain arrangements for him, yes.

00:31:48.630 --> 00:31:50.830
In return, I get protection.

00:31:50.830 --> 00:31:53.360
So this is Denny's wonderful brother.

00:31:53.360 --> 00:31:56.340
A fixer for a murdering Indian.

00:31:56.340 --> 00:32:00.000
You wouldn't call him that, do you?

00:32:00.280 --> 00:32:05.460
Sure, he's a savage, but kings have been savages too.

00:32:05.560 --> 00:32:08.070
- He's a guy-- - Don't move your hands.

00:32:08.170 --> 00:32:12.300
Maybe you could use a man like you, Water.

00:32:12.400 --> 00:32:14.660
Or are you happy in what you're doing?

00:32:14.760 --> 00:32:16.060
You could use me.

00:32:16.160 --> 00:32:18.260
Just keep very quiet and listen.

00:32:18.360 --> 00:32:20.710
You help me get that fella.

00:32:20.810 --> 00:32:22.170
You can get out of this hellhole.

00:32:22.270 --> 00:32:24.440
Spend your money on Broadway in New York.

00:32:24.540 --> 00:32:27.190
Or are you happy in what you're doing?

00:32:31.500 --> 00:32:35.030
- What protection can you offer me? - What protection can you offer me?

00:32:37.270 --> 00:32:38.840
Suppose I let you get out of this house.

00:32:40.110 --> 00:32:41.680
Meet me at the cantina in 10 minutes.

00:32:41.900 --> 00:32:45.270
- Where's the cantina? - Just down the street there.

00:32:47.070 --> 00:32:51.110
Get up out of that chair, mister.

00:32:52.100 --> 00:32:54.420
- Get over there between me and the door. - Right.

00:33:25.020 --> 00:33:25.570
Come on, Joe.

00:33:30.640 --> 00:33:38.800
keep going break up in two parties cut them off

00:34:20.570 --> 00:34:23.530
From now on, if I don't get a streetcar, I'm going to walk.

00:34:23.610 --> 00:34:25.910
Come on, Denny, we're temporarily dismounted.

00:34:25.970 --> 00:34:26.990
Hey, wait a minute, Joe.

00:34:27.070 --> 00:34:28.190
You're going to go back for more?

00:34:28.270 --> 00:34:30.000
I'm going back for a fellow named Eamon.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:43.510
Bring these Gringles in alive!

00:34:43.510 --> 00:34:47.150
Pablo, cover the North Road!

00:34:47.150 --> 00:34:49.590
Pancho, the South!

00:35:56.590 --> 00:36:00.000
Where are you going, Joe? We gotta go back and help Pat.

00:36:00.250 --> 00:36:02.270
in that big stone house the same way they got me.

00:36:02.570 --> 00:36:04.630
You got some bad news coming to you, cowboy.

00:36:04.980 --> 00:36:06.310
What do you mean I got some burdens?

00:36:11.770 --> 00:36:17.210
This is it. This fellow, the barber,

00:36:17.310 --> 00:36:19.040
he'll back up what I'm going to tell you.

00:36:22.370 --> 00:36:26.120
He's about the last honest man left in San Clemente.

00:36:30.380 --> 00:36:48.050
- Ricky! - A man in San Clemente.

00:36:48.050 --> 00:36:53.940
Let's get out of here, Joe. This guy's dead as a mackerel. I can't get used to him.

00:37:44.140 --> 00:37:44.880
- Just get out of here.

00:37:44.880 --> 00:37:48.570
- Just a minute.

00:37:48.570 --> 00:37:51.030
- I'll tell you this, son.

00:37:51.030 --> 00:37:52.390
I was tied up in that blanket.

00:37:52.390 --> 00:37:55.140
I was as close to L.T. Gray as his right-hand man.

00:37:55.140 --> 00:37:56.790
- You were?

00:37:56.790 --> 00:37:59.160
- His right-hand man was the old pride of 10th Avenue.

00:38:04.920 --> 00:38:11.370
- Patrick, I don't believe it.

00:38:11.370 --> 00:38:12.920
- But I saw him, Denny.

00:38:12.920 --> 00:38:14.350
I talked to him.

00:38:14.350 --> 00:38:17.500
That was his voice you heard, all right?

00:38:17.500 --> 00:38:23.420
- Can't be.

00:38:23.420 --> 00:38:25.200
- If you give yourself up,

00:38:25.200 --> 00:38:27.620
he'll see that you get back safe.

00:38:27.620 --> 00:38:28.870
He doesn't want to kill you.

00:38:30.160 --> 00:38:32.860
You're never gonna see him again.

00:38:32.860 --> 00:38:37.110
What do you wanna do?

00:38:37.110 --> 00:38:58.610
- Get these things off, Joe.

00:38:58.610 --> 00:39:00.000
- Time and a half, huh?

00:39:00.030 --> 00:39:05.780
against it I hope not because I've got a little job I want you to do where's the

00:39:05.780 --> 00:39:12.280
other one what other one tell the Gringo the one with the handcuffs who said

00:39:12.280 --> 00:39:15.450
there was another one with handcuffs everybody's in your everybody in San

00:39:15.450 --> 00:39:19.270
Clemente when I think it and mr. Omar speaks everybody in San Clemente listens

00:39:19.270 --> 00:39:23.600
and I have spoken tonight of you well that being the case we better put the

00:39:23.600 --> 00:39:30.000
cards right on the table come here Danny we've got to get these cuffs off mister

00:39:30.220 --> 00:39:36.340
- It looks to me like you're elected. - I'm afraid I don't do business at the point of a gun, senor.

00:39:36.780 --> 00:39:39.290
You're going to do business the way I tell you to tonight, partner.

00:39:40.090 --> 00:39:47.530
Go ahead, but just remember, at the sound of that gun, there will be 50 men here in 50 seconds.

00:39:48.010 --> 00:39:52.700
Each of them interested in collecting 10,000 pesos reward for you.

00:39:52.830 --> 00:39:56.180
- 10,000 pesos for me? - How much for me?

00:39:56.360 --> 00:40:00.000
- The same, senor. - Come on, Joe, let's take our business out.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:01.440
Wait a minute.

00:40:01.440 --> 00:40:05.020
How do you do business, partner?

00:40:05.020 --> 00:40:07.070
Put that gun down and I will tell you.

00:40:07.070 --> 00:40:09.340
Joe?

00:40:09.340 --> 00:40:11.190
Let's take a chance.

00:40:11.190 --> 00:40:14.380
Now, come here.

00:40:14.380 --> 00:40:17.960
Come here!

00:40:17.960 --> 00:40:20.680
You want those cops off, don't you?

00:40:20.680 --> 00:40:23.980
Sure, I want 'em off, but I don't want my head to be taken off with 'em.

00:40:23.980 --> 00:40:26.720
Now, hold very still.

00:40:26.720 --> 00:40:27.900
Wait a minute.

00:40:27.900 --> 00:40:30.000
All right.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:34.060
- All right.

00:40:34.060 --> 00:40:39.090
- Be careful.

00:40:39.090 --> 00:40:41.620
- Fine, but I still rattle when I eat.

00:40:41.620 --> 00:40:44.450
- Wait a minute, who's down there?

00:40:44.450 --> 00:40:47.130
- Be careful now, will ya?

00:40:47.130 --> 00:40:50.580
- Ow!

00:40:50.580 --> 00:40:54.350
- There it is!

00:40:54.350 --> 00:40:55.770
- Now the other one.

00:40:55.770 --> 00:40:57.970
- Come on, hurry it up, hurry it up.

00:41:28.160 --> 00:41:30.000
Don't you see two gringos this evening?

00:41:30.990 --> 00:41:32.790
- Get out of my light, you ox.

00:41:32.790 --> 00:41:35.090
- Be a little clever how you talk, Ortiz.

00:41:35.090 --> 00:41:42.190
- Then tell him to not get between me and my light.

00:41:42.190 --> 00:41:44.730
- Look, señor.

00:41:44.730 --> 00:41:47.480
- So you lied, eh?

00:41:47.480 --> 00:41:49.530
You cut these irons off a gringo?

00:41:49.530 --> 00:41:52.060
- Where did they go?

00:41:52.060 --> 00:41:54.160
- They didn't tell me and I didn't ask.

00:41:54.160 --> 00:41:55.440
Look in the corners.

00:41:55.440 --> 00:41:56.920
There's the street out there.

00:41:56.920 --> 00:41:58.500
Look in it.

00:41:58.500 --> 00:41:59.830
Here's the stable's yard.

00:42:00.280 --> 00:42:02.280
Well, then, that's the horses and mules.

00:42:02.380 --> 00:42:04.320
Maybe they can tell you where they went.

00:42:04.620 --> 00:42:06.020
Go ahead. Take a look.

00:42:43.210 --> 00:42:45.620
- How about this level? - Yeah.

00:43:01.880 --> 00:43:04.930
- This may go hard with you, Ortiz. - I know it.

00:43:04.930 --> 00:43:07.370
- What's here? - This, senor.

00:43:07.450 --> 00:43:14.970
- Who are you? - Enrico Ortiz, father of Pedro Ortiz.

00:43:15.050 --> 00:43:17.030
His son was killed during the last raid.

00:43:17.270 --> 00:43:23.370
My son was shot by a black-hearted swine and murderer who calls himself a tigre.

00:43:23.450 --> 00:43:28.110
- You're not entirely out of danger yourself, my friend. - On the contrary, senor.

00:43:28.130 --> 00:43:30.000
There's nothing whatever you can do to me.

00:43:30.570 --> 00:43:33.270
When my son died, I died.

00:43:33.270 --> 00:43:36.320
Keep him here.

00:43:36.320 --> 00:43:48.340
He's not here, senor.

00:43:48.340 --> 00:43:51.440
Father, hey, Roxie, senor.

00:43:51.440 --> 00:43:54.320
What about this?

00:43:54.320 --> 00:43:55.440
Not possibly.

00:43:55.440 --> 00:43:58.160
Give it.

00:44:05.280 --> 00:44:05.890
Let's go.

00:44:30.030 --> 00:44:30.770
Joe!

00:44:32.820 --> 00:44:33.820
Did you get your kid?

00:44:34.120 --> 00:44:35.970
He didn't exactly miss. Take it easy, Joe.

00:44:36.170 --> 00:44:37.790
Easy. Easy, Joe. Ow!

00:44:38.030 --> 00:44:38.960
Ow!

00:44:40.850 --> 00:44:41.850
Oh, it's all right.

00:44:42.630 --> 00:44:47.340
It's not too bad. That was him, all right.

00:44:48.470 --> 00:44:53.730
I was going to talk to him, Joe, but I got afraid.

00:44:54.000 --> 00:44:58.640
Can you imagine being afraid of your own brother?

00:45:06.400 --> 00:45:11.060
- They're gone now, senores.

00:45:11.060 --> 00:45:17.320
- Maria, get some flutin' coffee.

00:45:17.320 --> 00:45:18.920
- Yes, senor.

00:45:18.920 --> 00:45:22.710
- Let's have a look at that arm, Denny.

00:45:22.710 --> 00:45:24.340
- I think it's all right, Jill.

00:45:24.340 --> 00:45:26.030
It's beginning to bleed a little bit.

00:45:26.030 --> 00:45:27.450
- I got some oil and bandages.

00:45:27.450 --> 00:45:28.650
- Thank you.

00:45:28.650 --> 00:45:29.640
- Does it hurt, kid?

00:45:30.030 --> 00:45:37.590
I don't know what this stuff is, cowboy, so hang on.

00:45:37.590 --> 00:45:41.920
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! It burns!

00:45:41.920 --> 00:45:43.740
Ooh, it burns whatever it is.

00:45:43.740 --> 00:45:47.590
It's not very deep. Just nick the flesh.

00:45:47.590 --> 00:45:49.440
Whatever it nicked, it's burning.

00:45:49.440 --> 00:45:52.050
Say, Mr. Blacksmith. Yeah?

00:45:52.050 --> 00:45:54.130
I was listening to you out there.

00:45:54.130 --> 00:45:56.310
You sure got a lot of nerve, partner.

00:45:56.310 --> 00:45:58.200
Ain't you scared of nobody?

00:45:58.200 --> 00:46:00.000
Well, if they're scared of nobody, I'm not.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:01.000
You must fear that.

00:46:01.000 --> 00:46:02.550
Joe, I can't get it through my head.

00:46:02.550 --> 00:46:03.950
Pat, he's not this kind of a guy at all.

00:46:03.950 --> 00:46:04.950
He's not mean.

00:46:04.950 --> 00:46:05.890
Believe me.

00:46:05.890 --> 00:46:06.970
I know him.

00:46:06.970 --> 00:46:08.120
Something awful must have happened.

00:46:08.120 --> 00:46:09.120
And he can't get himself out of it.

00:46:09.120 --> 00:46:12.560
Maybe.

00:46:12.560 --> 00:46:15.080
Senorius?

00:46:15.080 --> 00:46:16.080
How about some food?

00:46:16.080 --> 00:46:17.080
Food?

00:46:17.080 --> 00:46:18.180
No thanks.

00:46:18.180 --> 00:46:19.320
No.

00:46:19.320 --> 00:46:21.320
Well, if I could only talk to him alone, I know I could get him to listen to me.

00:46:21.320 --> 00:46:26.480
Senor, besides the Tigre, there's only one person in the world Senor Amor might listen

00:46:26.480 --> 00:46:27.480
to.

00:46:27.480 --> 00:46:28.300
Who is this?

00:46:28.300 --> 00:46:29.210
The woman he's in love with.

00:46:29.210 --> 00:46:30.000
In love with?

00:46:30.700 --> 00:46:31.950
- Who is she?

00:46:31.950 --> 00:46:34.610
- The most beautiful senorita in San Clemente.

00:46:34.610 --> 00:46:35.830
Carmen Alvarado.

00:46:35.830 --> 00:46:37.860
- Carmel Alvarado.

00:46:37.860 --> 00:46:39.110
Have you ever seen her?

00:46:39.110 --> 00:46:41.760
- Yes, I have seen her.

00:46:41.760 --> 00:46:46.540
My son Pedro used to look at her with big eyes,

00:46:46.540 --> 00:46:50.960
but he was only a blacksmith, son.

00:46:50.960 --> 00:46:52.120
- Is she a big girl?

00:46:52.120 --> 00:46:55.920
- No, she's small and delicate.

00:46:55.920 --> 00:46:58.550
Your brother has a good taste anyhow.

00:46:58.550 --> 00:46:59.890
- Denny, how about some coffee?

00:47:00.480 --> 00:47:04.040
No, no thanks, Joe. I don't care for anything to drink.

00:47:04.040 --> 00:47:05.720
I feel...

00:47:05.720 --> 00:47:08.160
See, you haven't got a place that I could lie down for a little while, have you?

00:47:08.160 --> 00:47:08.820
Yeah.

00:47:08.820 --> 00:47:11.460
Maria, take this man out to my son's room.

00:47:11.460 --> 00:47:16.700
Si, senor.

00:47:16.700 --> 00:47:18.940
- Si, senor. - Yeah?

00:47:18.940 --> 00:47:21.360
You ever see this Mr. El Tigre yourself?

00:47:21.360 --> 00:47:28.640
No.

00:47:28.640 --> 00:47:29.880
Thank you. Gracias.

00:47:54.480 --> 00:47:55.000
We'll be right back.

00:48:13.560 --> 00:48:16.900
You know, the way I figure it, the best way we can thank you for what you've done

00:48:16.900 --> 00:48:20.730
is to clear out of here before some of them hobgoblins come calling on us.

00:48:20.730 --> 00:48:22.980
Oh, you're welcome to stay as long as you want.

00:48:22.980 --> 00:48:24.900
I'm not afraid of them.

00:48:24.900 --> 00:48:27.860
Man, you've got one slight advantage on me.

00:48:27.860 --> 00:48:29.350
You don't mind being killed.

00:49:08.160 --> 00:49:10.020
Well, I think I know what you mean.

00:49:10.460 --> 00:49:12.180
It's on the same road.

00:49:13.510 --> 00:49:14.150
Si, senor.

00:49:14.480 --> 00:49:15.770
But you waste your time.

00:49:17.990 --> 00:49:20.250
Senorita Alvarado has already been spoken for.

00:49:20.390 --> 00:49:22.810
Oh, I only want to speak to her on a little business.

00:49:23.660 --> 00:49:25.940
Perhaps after your business is true.

00:49:26.330 --> 00:49:27.770
You'll come back this way again?

00:49:28.590 --> 00:49:29.890
Well, I...

00:49:30.700 --> 00:49:32.200
I wouldn't count on it.

00:49:32.200 --> 00:49:36.360
- Muchas gracias, señorita. - I couldn't eat you yet.

00:49:36.360 --> 00:49:51.220
Patio.

00:49:51.220 --> 00:49:55.310
Cove de rico.

00:49:55.310 --> 00:49:57.310
Señorita.

00:49:57.310 --> 00:49:59.400
- It is a ghost. - A ghost?

00:50:01.400 --> 00:50:04.360
- Oh, let me see.

00:50:04.360 --> 00:50:17.830
- I shot him.

00:50:17.830 --> 00:50:22.320
- The rat.

00:50:22.320 --> 00:50:26.710
- Senorita.

00:50:26.710 --> 00:50:27.520
- Go to bed.

00:50:48.400 --> 00:50:52.020
- You are not dead, Pedro?

00:50:52.020 --> 00:50:56.400
- No, no, I'm no.

00:50:56.400 --> 00:51:00.000
- You are not Pedro Ortiz.

00:51:01.120 --> 00:51:04.380
I want to talk to you, about my brother.

00:51:04.380 --> 00:51:05.930
- How did you get in here?

00:51:05.930 --> 00:51:08.010
Go away or I will call to God.

00:51:08.010 --> 00:51:10.480
- I'm not gonna go away, my name is Denny.

00:51:10.480 --> 00:51:13.880
Dennis O'Moore.

00:51:13.880 --> 00:51:14.920
- O'Moore?

00:51:14.920 --> 00:51:16.220
- Yes, look, if you're not gonna come down,

00:51:16.220 --> 00:51:18.040
I'm gonna climb up there and talk to you.

00:51:18.040 --> 00:51:21.020
- No, no, no, no, please, please.

00:51:21.020 --> 00:51:22.360
I will come down there.

00:51:22.360 --> 00:51:24.640
You wait a minute, get out of sight.

00:52:07.100 --> 00:52:08.580
You are Senor Ambo's brother?

00:52:09.180 --> 00:52:09.500
Yeah.

00:52:10.980 --> 00:52:12.650
He's a girl to believe.

00:52:12.890 --> 00:52:14.550
Oh, maybe it's the clothes.

00:52:14.790 --> 00:52:15.610
They aren't mine.

00:52:15.890 --> 00:52:17.410
I had to get them from the blacksmith's house.

00:52:18.410 --> 00:52:18.950
You see, I...

00:52:18.950 --> 00:52:28.450
What you wish to say about your brother?

00:52:29.020 --> 00:52:29.700
Hey, you're...

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:32.060
- You're a little, aren't you?

00:52:32.060 --> 00:52:33.400
- I beg your pardon?

00:52:33.400 --> 00:52:37.290
- Oh, I mean, you're, uh, you're parquito.

00:52:37.290 --> 00:52:38.830
- Uh-huh.

00:52:38.830 --> 00:52:40.810
- Small, you know, small.

00:52:40.810 --> 00:52:44.970
- Si, but you're not much taller than I am.

00:52:44.970 --> 00:52:47.020
- I know, but I've been used to whoppers.

00:52:47.020 --> 00:52:47.860
- Eh?

00:52:47.860 --> 00:52:49.740
- Big girls, big girls.

00:52:49.740 --> 00:52:52.140
I've been out with some regular whales.

00:52:52.140 --> 00:52:53.260
In fact, I've never even talked to a girl

00:52:53.260 --> 00:52:55.810
that was under six feet tall.

00:52:55.810 --> 00:52:58.460
- Uh, you wish to talk about your brother?

00:52:58.460 --> 00:52:59.380
- Yes.

00:53:00.160 --> 00:53:03.460
That's why I wanted to talk to you, senorita. Yes.

00:53:03.800 --> 00:53:05.560
Why did you come to me?

00:53:05.660 --> 00:53:07.940
Well, I'm in trouble, and I don't understand it.

00:53:08.030 --> 00:53:10.600
I thought maybe you could explain what all this means.

00:53:10.930 --> 00:53:16.930
Yes, but please be quiet. Tell me, what do you mean?

00:53:17.320 --> 00:53:21.400
Well, you see, senorita, Patrick was the best thing in our family.

00:53:21.500 --> 00:53:23.250
The best thing on 10th Avenue, for that matter.

00:53:23.480 --> 00:53:27.250
The one we were always bragging about, the one we were always so proud of.

00:53:27.670 --> 00:53:28.960
You know what I mean, don't you?

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:32.550
- Yes, I hear what you are saying, but...

00:53:32.550 --> 00:53:34.610
- Tonight, you almost killed me with that pitchfork.

00:53:34.610 --> 00:53:36.870
My own brother, why you wouldn't have believed it.

00:53:36.870 --> 00:53:39.230
- That I can't believe.

00:53:39.230 --> 00:53:40.690
What did you say your name was?

00:53:40.690 --> 00:53:44.230
- Denny, Dennis O'Moore.

00:53:44.230 --> 00:53:46.110
- But you're so different from your brother.

00:53:46.110 --> 00:53:48.470
- Oh, I never was much compared to Patrick.

00:53:48.470 --> 00:53:50.310
He was always tall and good-looking, and me, I...

00:53:50.310 --> 00:53:52.010
- Oh, but I didn't mean that.

00:53:52.010 --> 00:53:56.930
I was thinking of something every time.

00:53:56.930 --> 00:53:59.600
- How much do you weigh?

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:03.610
- Will you please stop measuring me.

00:54:03.610 --> 00:54:11.400
- Well, you know, I feel better about Patrick already.

00:54:11.400 --> 00:54:14.110
- How?

00:54:14.110 --> 00:54:17.500
- Well, just knowing that a girl like you

00:54:17.500 --> 00:54:18.900
is in love with him.

00:54:18.900 --> 00:54:22.730
- Oh, but you're wrong, I don't love him.

00:54:22.730 --> 00:54:24.540
- Don't love him?

00:54:24.540 --> 00:54:27.940
- Oh no, I hate him, I'm afraid of him.

00:54:30.090 --> 00:54:31.590
He's crazy.

00:54:31.590 --> 00:54:34.040
Patrick?

00:54:34.040 --> 00:54:35.830
Listen, senor.

00:54:35.830 --> 00:54:38.170
I am not the superstitious peasant girl,

00:54:38.170 --> 00:54:42.400
but I tell you an evil spirit has entered his soul.

00:54:42.400 --> 00:54:49.580
He is, uh, possessed.

00:54:49.580 --> 00:54:54.690
He's waiting.

00:54:54.690 --> 00:54:57.250
Maybe this fellow, Altigri, has got something on him.

00:54:57.250 --> 00:55:00.000
Maybe Patrick got himself into trouble and this guy helped him out and...

00:55:00.090 --> 00:55:02.470
He's got a hold on him and Patrick can't help himself.

00:55:02.470 --> 00:55:03.710
That's why I wanted to talk to you,

00:55:03.710 --> 00:55:05.090
to make him come back with me,

00:55:05.090 --> 00:55:06.250
to beg him to come back with me.

00:55:06.250 --> 00:55:24.540
- Shh.

00:55:24.540 --> 00:55:25.660
- Good evening.

00:55:25.660 --> 00:55:27.210
- You have a man in this garden, where is he?

00:55:27.210 --> 00:55:28.450
- I haven't the slightest intention

00:55:28.450 --> 00:55:30.000
of answering a question like that.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:31.000
I'll be out of your mind.

00:55:31.000 --> 00:55:37.490
Patrick, Patrick, this is what I've been waiting for a chance to talk to you.

00:55:37.490 --> 00:55:40.940
What goes on here with you?

00:55:40.940 --> 00:55:42.710
You devil.

00:55:42.710 --> 00:55:43.630
Go in the house, senorita.

00:55:43.630 --> 00:55:44.630
What are you going to do to him?

00:55:44.630 --> 00:55:46.540
You leave that to me, if you please.

00:55:46.540 --> 00:55:47.550
All right.

00:55:47.550 --> 00:55:48.550
Did you hear me?

00:55:48.550 --> 00:55:50.170
Get inside.

00:55:50.170 --> 00:55:53.720
All right.

00:55:53.720 --> 00:55:55.610
Let's close out his.

00:55:55.610 --> 00:55:57.950
Take a look and see if you can identify them.

00:55:57.950 --> 00:55:59.730
They may give us a line on Mr. Warder.

00:56:01.660 --> 00:56:05.780
- He's worse than 10th Avenue.

00:56:05.780 --> 00:56:07.000
- Better get going, son.

00:56:07.000 --> 00:56:20.010
Danny, it's time to get any clothes in that room.

00:56:20.010 --> 00:56:23.510
- Well, there were some of my sons.

00:56:23.510 --> 00:56:25.310
- Oh, then that's it.

00:56:25.310 --> 00:56:26.760
For a minute, I was wondering what he went out in.

00:56:34.670 --> 00:56:36.630
- Who is it? - Let me in quickly.

00:56:36.630 --> 00:56:39.380
It's Yuri Paraborado.

00:56:39.380 --> 00:56:44.770
- Lyren. - Have you seen your walk?

00:56:44.770 --> 00:56:47.700
- Yes. - Your friend, Denny is in trouble.

00:56:47.700 --> 00:56:49.700
They're taking him to El Tivre.

00:56:49.700 --> 00:56:51.700
- Who got him? Patrick? - Si.

00:56:51.700 --> 00:56:54.530
Now they're looking for you. I heard them talking.

00:56:54.530 --> 00:56:57.310
- Did Denny tell them anything? - My word.

00:56:57.310 --> 00:57:00.000
- He would have to. - It was his son Pedro's good suit he wore.

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:02.050
Oh, they'd know where he came from?

00:57:02.050 --> 00:57:04.650
Put out that light, senor.

00:57:04.650 --> 00:57:06.830
What do you think you can do?

00:57:06.830 --> 00:57:21.580
Out of sight. They won't bother you.

00:57:21.580 --> 00:57:26.300
Give me that gun. But they're not after you.

00:57:26.300 --> 00:57:28.390
You stay clean.

00:57:31.720 --> 00:57:33.920
And when I get upstairs, you go to the door with your hands up.

00:57:37.230 --> 00:57:40.950
Either you open up, senor, or I'll have to blow the lock off.

00:57:42.250 --> 00:57:43.410
Good evening, my friend.

00:57:48.020 --> 00:57:49.110
Where is senor Warder?

00:57:49.270 --> 00:57:50.260
Look for yourself.

00:57:51.220 --> 00:57:52.400
Upstairs, eh?

00:57:54.620 --> 00:57:55.760
All right, amigos.

00:57:56.360 --> 00:57:58.710
Ten thousand pesos at the top of the stairs.

00:57:58.940 --> 00:57:59.700
Who's first?

00:58:00.990 --> 00:58:03.040
Why don't you send this donkey out?

00:58:03.040 --> 00:58:04.960
He is a fearless man.

00:58:04.960 --> 00:58:05.990
Who wants to go?

00:58:05.990 --> 00:58:07.390
I'll go, Capitan.

00:58:07.390 --> 00:58:08.390
No, no.

00:58:08.390 --> 00:58:09.390
I have a better idea.

00:58:09.390 --> 00:58:12.560
I prefer to take this great ranger without violence.

00:58:12.560 --> 00:58:13.510
Come here, please.

00:58:13.510 --> 00:58:18.400
Turn around, please.

00:58:18.400 --> 00:58:22.770
Senor Warder.

00:58:22.770 --> 00:58:25.430
Can you hear me, Senor Warder?

00:58:25.430 --> 00:58:27.450
I have my gun on Senor Ortiz's back.

00:58:27.450 --> 00:58:29.480
If I don't hear from you by the time I count three...

00:58:30.060 --> 00:58:34.650
It'll be the end of him.

00:58:34.650 --> 00:58:37.260
One, two.

00:58:37.260 --> 00:58:39.500
Pay attention to him, amigo.

00:58:39.500 --> 00:58:40.700
Three.

00:58:40.700 --> 00:58:42.610
All right, you win.

00:58:42.610 --> 00:58:51.590
Throw out your gun first.

00:58:51.590 --> 00:58:58.860
Both of them, if you please.

00:58:58.860 --> 00:59:00.000
Now come down with your hands.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:11.460
Thank you very much.

00:59:11.460 --> 00:59:16.740
Now you dirty gringo.

00:59:16.740 --> 00:59:23.120
Our friend is a little drunk this evening.

00:59:23.120 --> 00:59:26.970
Apparently you shouldn't pick on men smaller than yourself, amigo.

00:59:26.970 --> 00:59:28.930
Wait outside.

00:59:30.440 --> 00:59:31.770
- Tie him up.

00:59:31.770 --> 00:59:33.460
- I'll be a good boy, mister.

00:59:33.460 --> 00:59:36.120
- I'm sorry, senor, but your reflexes are much too dangerous.

00:59:36.120 --> 00:59:37.720
I'd rather not take the chance.

00:59:37.720 --> 00:59:38.540
- What about Ortiz?

00:59:38.540 --> 00:59:39.420
He hasn't done anything.

00:59:39.420 --> 00:59:41.580
- And we're going to see that he doesn't either.

00:59:41.580 --> 00:59:48.020
Outside, please.

00:59:48.020 --> 00:59:51.420
- I think you'd better take me too, senor.

00:59:51.420 --> 00:59:53.850
I also have business with Patrick O'Moore.

00:59:53.850 --> 00:59:56.050
- With the greatest of pleasure, senorita.

01:00:32.560 --> 01:00:33.860
- Is the Capitan here?

01:00:33.860 --> 01:00:35.660
- No, Senor, nobody.

01:00:35.660 --> 01:00:44.840
- All right, get off.

01:00:44.840 --> 01:01:00.000
- You don't take a hinting

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:06.300
easily, do you, Denny? All right, you're here. You wanted to talk to me, so talk. How's

01:01:06.300 --> 01:01:10.760
mother? How's Mamie? How are they getting along? This is wonderful. First of all, you

01:01:10.760 --> 01:01:13.840
hire a bunch of thugs to chase me around with guns. Your partner killed me with a pitchfork.

01:01:14.220 --> 01:01:17.600
You cold cocked me on the jaw when I owed my arms to you. And now you're a big family

01:01:17.600 --> 01:01:20.440
man. Mother's Day boy. I need you to protect you, to keep your mouth shut. Well, don't

01:01:20.440 --> 01:01:23.810
do me any favors, will you, please? I told you not to come down here. This is my life.

01:01:23.870 --> 01:01:28.130
Stay out of it. I've taken care of you and the family. The O'Mores don't want any money

01:01:28.130 --> 01:01:30.000
from robberies or murders. The O'Mores family isn't

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:31.740
I'm gonna know what you think you know.

01:01:31.740 --> 01:01:36.420
If you go back, you're gonna keep quiet.

01:01:36.420 --> 01:01:38.250
You see, Danny?

01:01:38.250 --> 01:01:41.560
There's some things you don't understand.

01:01:41.560 --> 01:01:44.250
- Like L. Tigre, for instance?

01:01:44.250 --> 01:01:46.240
Well, Pat, what's this guy got on you?

01:01:46.240 --> 01:01:47.740
- He saved my life once.

01:01:47.740 --> 01:01:51.260
Now he, now he controls it.

01:01:51.260 --> 01:01:52.800
- Controls it? I don't understand it.

01:01:52.800 --> 01:01:53.940
Has he got you hypnotized or something?

01:01:53.940 --> 01:01:55.700
- I don't know.

01:01:55.700 --> 01:01:57.520
You don't understand power, what it does to you.

01:01:57.520 --> 01:01:59.000
- I know you could get away from here if you wanted to.

01:01:59.000 --> 01:01:59.600
- Maybe.

01:02:00.220 --> 01:02:04.110
- Someday, and be afraid to try now.

01:02:04.110 --> 01:02:05.870
- Afraid, are you afraid?

01:02:05.870 --> 01:02:07.630
You can't kid me, you're not afraid of anything.

01:02:07.630 --> 01:02:08.610
Don't tell me that you're afraid--

01:02:08.610 --> 01:02:09.910
- Shut up!

01:02:09.910 --> 01:02:11.520
I know where I'm going.

01:02:11.520 --> 01:02:12.600
- Are you sure it's only that Indian

01:02:12.600 --> 01:02:14.340
that's keeping you here?

01:02:14.340 --> 01:02:17.950
How about that Carmel Alvarado?

01:02:17.950 --> 01:02:19.340
- What about her?

01:02:19.340 --> 01:02:21.060
- You can't force a girl to marry you.

01:02:21.060 --> 01:02:21.900
- Marriage is different here.

01:02:21.900 --> 01:02:23.580
Marriage is for position to be a place in the world.

01:02:23.580 --> 01:02:24.760
- But she doesn't love you, she hates you,

01:02:24.760 --> 01:02:28.350
she thinks you're nuts.

01:02:28.350 --> 01:02:29.120
- Did she tell you that?

01:02:32.720 --> 01:02:34.720
- I said, did she tell you that?

01:02:34.720 --> 01:02:36.140
Why don't you put it in her head?

01:02:41.600 --> 01:02:42.890
- Put him upstairs.

01:02:42.890 --> 01:02:50.910
Lock him inside.

01:02:50.910 --> 01:02:51.570
Come on, let's go.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:10.940
- Discount, senores, and senorita.

01:03:10.940 --> 01:03:16.470
As ordered, el senor plus one lady.

01:03:16.470 --> 01:03:17.660
- What's she doing here?

01:03:17.660 --> 01:03:19.500
- I insisted, senor.

01:03:19.500 --> 01:03:21.850
Would you care to discuss your reason here?

01:03:21.850 --> 01:03:23.970
- I came to this town with a good kid named Denny

01:03:23.970 --> 01:03:25.770
and a good horse named Sonny.

01:03:25.770 --> 01:03:27.880
Take good care of both of them, cowboy.

01:03:27.880 --> 01:03:28.640
Put 'em in the box.

01:03:30.440 --> 01:03:54.100
- Come here. - We've got these ropes on our hands, amigo.

01:03:54.250 --> 01:03:56.980
Come on, get inside. Come on.

01:04:03.290 --> 01:04:07.700
- This looks like the one dollar room.

01:04:07.700 --> 01:04:08.900
- But I beg of you, senorita.

01:04:08.900 --> 01:04:11.510
- There's no need of any further discussion, senorita.

01:04:11.510 --> 01:04:14.550
What I decide to do with my brother is no business of yours.

01:04:14.550 --> 01:04:15.910
I'm sending you back to San Clemente.

01:04:15.910 --> 01:04:18.910
- Your brother came to me only because he was concerned about you.

01:04:18.910 --> 01:04:20.410
He wanted me to reassure him.

01:04:20.410 --> 01:04:22.330
- Which you did, of course.

01:04:22.330 --> 01:04:25.750
- What I told him about you was difficult for him to believe.

01:04:25.750 --> 01:04:29.320
Until you arrived and confirmed it with such grace and charm.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:33.360
- My brother won't bother you in your garden anymore.

01:04:33.360 --> 01:04:36.900
- Are you a little crazy, senor?

01:04:36.900 --> 01:04:41.470
- Don't ever say that, again.

01:04:41.470 --> 01:04:48.240
Capitan, senorita Alvarado's atoning to her home.

01:04:48.240 --> 01:04:49.920
I want you to ride back with her.

01:04:49.920 --> 01:04:52.210
- That'll be an honor, senorita.

01:04:52.210 --> 01:04:53.880
- The horses, please.

01:04:53.880 --> 01:04:55.840
- Tell senora Alvarado to take better care

01:04:55.840 --> 01:04:57.080
of my fiance.

01:04:57.080 --> 01:04:58.320
- I certainly will, senor.

01:05:15.870 --> 01:05:24.410
Just and easy.

01:05:24.410 --> 01:05:25.090
I brought your anvil.

01:05:31.080 --> 01:05:48.790
- They are so stiff. - Get out. Give me the key and get out.

01:05:49.020 --> 01:05:52.080
Yes, sir.

01:06:01.210 --> 01:06:06.150
- Where? - The dunk is back.

01:06:30.030 --> 01:06:32.720
Arch! Arch!

01:07:01.340 --> 01:07:19.650
It was a gun, a gag on it.

01:07:19.650 --> 01:07:23.810
- Porter and the other man. - Yes, senora.

01:07:36.330 --> 01:07:56.040
- How about this? - Oh, now, don't get opened.

01:07:56.040 --> 01:08:00.000
Yeah, we had a visit from a fellow named Berger.

01:08:00.920 --> 01:08:03.330
- All right, come on.

01:08:03.330 --> 01:08:06.890
- You too.

01:08:06.890 --> 01:08:07.930
- Easy, muchachos.

01:08:07.930 --> 01:08:10.950
When I want you to be rough, I'll tell you.

01:08:10.950 --> 01:08:13.330
- Jenny, being my brother's that you get away

01:08:13.330 --> 01:08:15.360
with all you're gonna get away with.

01:08:15.360 --> 01:08:16.760
- El Tigre's on his way here.

01:08:16.760 --> 01:08:17.950
- El Tigre?

01:08:17.950 --> 01:08:22.220
Oh, that makes me just shaking my boots.

01:08:22.220 --> 01:08:23.590
Joe!

01:08:23.590 --> 01:08:26.680
- Sorry, partner.

01:08:26.680 --> 01:08:28.750
- El, it's a nice place here.

01:08:28.750 --> 01:08:29.760
- They got you too.

01:08:30.220 --> 01:08:31.560
- Makes a kind of cozy, don't it?

01:08:31.560 --> 01:08:32.450
- What's Berger?

01:08:32.450 --> 01:08:33.290
- I don't know, senor.

01:08:33.290 --> 01:08:34.220
- Go find him.

01:08:34.220 --> 01:08:37.620
- Yes, senor.

01:08:37.620 --> 01:08:38.940
- Now listen, we can make a deal,

01:08:38.940 --> 01:08:39.900
but it's got to be fast.

01:08:39.900 --> 01:08:40.900
I may be exceeding my authority.

01:08:40.900 --> 01:08:41.700
- What kind of a deal?

01:08:41.700 --> 01:08:43.280
- You're going back over the border tonight, Denny.

01:08:43.280 --> 01:08:44.440
- I am, and for how long?

01:08:44.440 --> 01:08:45.950
- That's where the deal comes in.

01:08:45.950 --> 01:08:47.790
If you give me a word to keep your mouth shut back home

01:08:47.790 --> 01:08:51.090
and never to come back, you can take water with you.

01:08:51.090 --> 01:08:52.750
- And if I don't?

01:08:52.750 --> 01:08:55.770
- I'll have to take care of Mr. Water some other way.

01:08:55.770 --> 01:08:58.110
- Gee, Joe, this kind of leaves me

01:08:58.110 --> 01:08:59.640
in an embarrassing position.

01:09:00.480 --> 01:09:02.370
- You see, there's a young lady involved.

01:09:02.370 --> 01:09:05.200
- Oh, I might have known.

01:09:05.200 --> 01:09:06.700
- How about him?

01:09:06.700 --> 01:09:09.070
- You and the water don't belong here, Ortiz does.

01:09:09.070 --> 01:09:10.010
You can forget about him.

01:09:10.010 --> 01:09:10.850
- Now, wait just a minute.

01:09:10.850 --> 01:09:11.690
We all got in this thing together,

01:09:11.690 --> 01:09:12.860
and we're all gonna get out of it together.

01:09:12.860 --> 01:09:15.060
Ortiz, Joe, myself, and Carmelita, there's no deal.

01:09:15.060 --> 01:09:15.900
Is that right, Joe?

01:09:15.900 --> 01:09:17.140
- Well, I might be a little prejudiced

01:09:17.140 --> 01:09:18.740
in favor of staying alive.

01:09:18.740 --> 01:09:20.820
You see, I ain't met Miss Carmelita yet.

01:09:20.820 --> 01:09:22.560
How did you meet her?

01:09:22.560 --> 01:09:23.860
- Never mind how I met her.

01:09:23.860 --> 01:09:25.350
- I said, how did you meet her?

01:09:25.350 --> 01:09:26.510
- Look, I'm getting a little tired

01:09:26.510 --> 01:09:27.590
of getting pushed around here.

01:09:27.590 --> 01:09:28.960
- Did she ask you to that garden?

01:09:28.960 --> 01:09:30.000
Get that chair down!

01:09:30.510 --> 01:09:31.970
- Get away from me, will you?

01:09:31.970 --> 01:09:39.120
- Omar, tell them not to shoot quick.

01:09:39.120 --> 01:09:41.960
Take it easy, men.

01:09:41.960 --> 01:09:43.690
Now tell them to put their guns on the floor.

01:09:43.690 --> 01:09:45.360
Just a minute, Ortiz.

01:09:45.360 --> 01:09:47.510
Don't drop 'em, lay 'em down.

01:09:47.510 --> 01:09:50.690
- Go ahead, do what he says.

01:09:50.690 --> 01:09:53.250
- Go ahead, do what my brother said, drop that gun.

01:09:53.250 --> 01:09:54.090
- Don't drop it.

01:09:54.090 --> 01:09:55.420
- Don't drop it.

01:09:55.420 --> 01:09:56.760
- Put it down easy.

01:09:56.760 --> 01:09:58.640
- Put it down easy, go on.

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:02.650
- Now call them outside fellas in.

01:10:02.650 --> 01:10:03.780
- Pablo.

01:10:03.780 --> 01:10:07.090
- Go.

01:10:07.090 --> 01:10:10.200
- Hey, the senor say come in here.

01:10:10.200 --> 01:10:20.920
- Pronto.

01:10:20.920 --> 01:10:21.920
- Tell him to reach.

01:10:21.920 --> 01:10:23.460
- Put him up.

01:10:23.460 --> 01:10:25.410
- Danny, you and Ortiz get their guns.

01:10:25.410 --> 01:10:26.290
- Right.

01:10:26.290 --> 01:10:27.760
All right, come on you guys, in the hat.

01:10:27.760 --> 01:10:28.490
Let's go.

01:10:28.490 --> 01:10:30.000
You have to make it snappy, let's go.

01:10:31.850 --> 01:10:35.150
Holdin' out, huh?

01:10:35.150 --> 01:10:36.650
Well, I got 'em all, Joe. What'll I do with 'em?

01:10:36.650 --> 01:10:38.050
Chuck 'em out that window.

01:10:38.050 --> 01:10:40.460
Seems like an awful waste of weapons.

01:10:40.460 --> 01:10:41.960
Ortiz, get that other bunch over here.

01:10:41.960 --> 01:10:44.700
Come on!

01:10:44.700 --> 01:10:46.090
Come on!

01:10:46.090 --> 01:10:48.810
Hey, Sunshine, are you sure this is all?

01:10:48.810 --> 01:10:50.110
I think so, senor.

01:10:50.110 --> 01:10:51.730
Well, you better be sure, cowboy.

01:10:51.730 --> 01:10:53.830
'Cause if you ain't, you're gonna be short one boss.

01:10:53.830 --> 01:10:55.030
I am sure, senor.

01:10:55.030 --> 01:10:56.540
All right, then, everybody over in that corner.

01:10:56.540 --> 01:10:57.440
Hurry after him!

01:10:57.440 --> 01:10:59.440
Everybody but you, cowboy. You're goin' with us.

01:10:59.440 --> 01:11:00.000
Denny!

01:11:00.220 --> 01:11:02.520
You and Ortiz get some horses. Four good ones.

01:11:02.520 --> 01:11:04.540
Gotcha.

01:11:04.540 --> 01:11:08.440
All you gotta do is just back up easy when I say so.

01:11:08.440 --> 01:11:11.470
Come on. You're gonna be all right. Come on.

01:11:11.470 --> 01:11:14.250
Now the rest of you just take it easy, that's all.

01:11:14.250 --> 01:11:15.840
Don't make no sudden moves.

01:11:33.450 --> 01:11:35.310
Mr. Ortiz stampede those other horses.

01:11:35.310 --> 01:11:36.310
Give me the ropes.

01:11:36.310 --> 01:11:39.280
Cut them loose and fire a couple of shots.

01:12:30.160 --> 01:12:31.420
- Where did you come from?

01:12:31.420 --> 01:12:33.000
- El Capitan left me here.

01:12:33.000 --> 01:12:56.430
- Come on, let's get going.

01:12:56.430 --> 01:12:57.290
Where's Ortiz?

01:12:57.290 --> 01:12:58.420
- I thought he was ahead of us.

01:12:58.420 --> 01:13:00.000
- Look, you two better cut away

01:13:00.030 --> 01:13:01.030
I'm the one they're really after.

01:13:01.030 --> 01:13:01.950
Save your breath.

01:13:01.950 --> 01:13:02.950
We're in this thing together.

01:13:02.950 --> 01:13:03.940
Here he comes.

01:13:03.940 --> 01:13:06.730
Come on.

01:13:41.260 --> 01:13:42.920
Not your brother.

01:13:42.920 --> 01:13:53.780
It's me.

01:13:53.780 --> 01:13:55.030
There was nothing you could do to me.

01:14:09.050 --> 01:14:11.710
I sure hope so. This horse of mine's getting lame awful fast.

01:14:11.710 --> 01:14:13.830
I've taken about all this riding I can.

01:14:30.830 --> 01:14:31.470
You all right, Denny?

01:14:31.570 --> 01:14:34.080
Yeah, I am, but my horse ain't.

01:14:34.920 --> 01:14:36.040
I should have got that other fella.

01:14:36.080 --> 01:14:37.400
He's going to turn out to be a tattletale.

01:14:37.870 --> 01:14:38.270
That's right.

01:14:38.310 --> 01:14:39.510
We'll need the rifle and bandolier.

01:14:39.690 --> 01:14:40.230
Where are we going?

01:14:40.740 --> 01:14:42.040
That looks like a nice little place.

01:14:42.100 --> 01:14:42.880
Go see if it's for rent.

01:14:43.660 --> 01:14:51.480
Come on, let's get out of here.

01:15:02.590 --> 01:15:05.410
Well, this is worse than it looked. No plumbing.

01:15:05.440 --> 01:15:06.300
Yeah.

01:15:06.550 --> 01:15:08.450
Say, Joe, how far is it to the border?

01:15:08.550 --> 01:15:09.760
It's a long way.

01:15:10.070 --> 01:15:11.700
- Well, look, Carmel, maybe you'll... - Oh, what'd I tell you?

01:15:11.800 --> 01:15:26.300
Look, what do you suppose this fellow's up to?

01:15:31.340 --> 01:15:33.330
- It's El Capitan.

01:15:33.330 --> 01:15:36.790
- Say, I've seen this guy someplace before.

01:15:36.790 --> 01:15:42.790
- I apologize, señorita.

01:15:42.790 --> 01:15:43.840
- Is that what you come for?

01:15:43.840 --> 01:15:45.050
- Not altogether.

01:15:45.050 --> 01:15:48.110
I was also wondering if you'd care to surrender.

01:15:48.110 --> 01:15:49.730
- What good would that do us?

01:15:49.730 --> 01:15:52.000
- The offer to return you to the border still holds good,

01:15:52.000 --> 01:15:54.220
I understand, barring accidents.

01:15:54.220 --> 01:15:55.810
- Barring accidents?

01:15:55.810 --> 01:15:57.330
- I don't think my captain would like it

01:15:57.330 --> 01:15:59.570
if I was delivered back to him accidentally killed.

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:01.800
- What about Senorita Alvarado?

01:16:01.800 --> 01:16:04.590
- Tell Senor Amor that we do not trust his offer.

01:16:04.590 --> 01:16:06.390
I am here with Senor Danny and Senor Water,

01:16:06.390 --> 01:16:07.990
and I intend to stay here.

01:16:07.990 --> 01:16:09.850
Let him decide what to do about that.

01:16:09.850 --> 01:16:11.710
- Unfortunately, Senorita,

01:16:11.710 --> 01:16:14.830
it's no longer a matter for Senor Amor to decide.

01:16:14.830 --> 01:16:17.290
It is now in the hands of El Tigre.

01:16:17.290 --> 01:16:20.340
- All right then, tell him to come get us.

01:16:20.340 --> 01:16:21.440
- Very well.

01:16:21.440 --> 01:16:23.560
In that case, you're gonna need more ammunition.

01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:31.820
I hope you'll be good enough not to use it

01:16:31.820 --> 01:16:34.210
until I've reached some kind of protection.

01:16:34.210 --> 01:16:35.510
Adios, señorita.

01:16:35.510 --> 01:16:46.770
Amigos?

01:16:46.770 --> 01:16:54.650
Say, what side is that guy on?

01:16:54.650 --> 01:16:55.830
- Annie. - Joe.

01:17:00.380 --> 01:17:02.910
- They're up to something.

01:17:02.910 --> 01:17:03.750
- His nibs?

01:17:03.750 --> 01:17:04.590
- Yeah.

01:17:06.330 --> 01:17:09.150
- What do we do, just bang away at him?

01:17:09.150 --> 01:17:11.100
- Well, we might be able to discourage him a little.

01:17:11.100 --> 01:17:18.340
Here, Carmel.

01:17:18.340 --> 01:17:21.610
- Now I'll be a son of a gun.

01:17:21.610 --> 01:17:23.870
That looks like Sonny he's on.

01:17:23.870 --> 01:17:26.350
- Sonny, your horse?

01:17:26.350 --> 01:17:27.650
- That dirty horse thief.

01:17:30.280 --> 01:17:33.790
Hey, wait a minute. Just a minute now.

01:17:36.740 --> 01:17:37.260
What is it?

01:17:37.920 --> 01:17:41.570
We may be able to finally have a little get-together with that fellow El Tigre.

01:17:42.260 --> 01:17:43.930
If we get him, we've got a chance.

01:17:46.750 --> 01:17:58.390
Wait for the signal. Come on!

01:18:11.290 --> 01:18:12.000
Go, Joe, now!

01:19:17.440 --> 01:19:18.560
Are you all right, Joe?

01:19:18.560 --> 01:19:19.620
Yeah, I think so.

01:19:19.620 --> 01:19:27.560
Pretty close, eh?

01:19:27.560 --> 01:19:30.000
Myself, I don't like it that close.

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:31.900
I don't like it close at all.

01:19:32.000 --> 01:19:34.300
Just how do you like it, cowboy?

01:19:34.400 --> 01:19:35.300
I'm not a hero, amigo.

01:19:35.400 --> 01:19:39.250
I'm just a practical policeman from the Secret Service Bureau in Mexico City.

01:19:39.350 --> 01:19:45.990
And I do not try to make an arrest until I know I can get my prisoner back to the calaboo safely.

01:19:46.090 --> 01:19:47.960
I get it.

01:19:48.060 --> 01:19:51.460
You see those old fellas chasing my old comrades in crime?

01:19:51.560 --> 01:19:57.490
For a long time, we've all been waiting for just such an opportunity as this.

01:19:57.590 --> 01:20:00.000
Thank you, senores, for your time.

01:20:00.030 --> 01:20:05.640
wonderful cooperation and much obliged to you colonel sanchez for yours not at all have you

01:20:05.640 --> 01:20:11.270
examined our friend over here very interesting chap you should take a close look at him

01:20:39.920 --> 01:20:41.430
I have to tell the kid.

01:21:01.280 --> 01:21:05.400
- Could've got me easy.

01:21:05.400 --> 01:21:09.410
- Sorry it was your brother, Denny.

01:21:09.410 --> 01:21:16.260
- My brother died a long time ago, Joe.

01:21:16.260 --> 01:21:18.260
- I'll take over from here, Ranger.

01:21:18.260 --> 01:21:19.720
Your friend can take my horse.

01:21:19.720 --> 01:21:20.560
- Thanks.

01:21:20.560 --> 01:21:21.800
- You have a long ride ahead.

01:21:21.800 --> 01:21:23.810
- Yeah, Colonel, it's been a right busy day.

01:21:30.090 --> 01:21:32.460
Gracias.

01:21:32.460 --> 01:21:35.180
Well, how far do you plan we shall go in this manner?

01:21:35.180 --> 01:21:36.880
Maybe a long way, senorita.

01:21:36.880 --> 01:21:40.370
You see, you're the first girl I've ever been able to lift.
